From: PC110 Web <pc110-web@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] emscripten: allow wasm32 system emulator configuration

QEMU's generic 32-bit host guard rejects the Emscripten wasm32 target before
the web backend and interpreter configuration can be validated. Keep the guard
for native 32-bit hosts, but permit the explicitly supported Emscripten route.

---
 meson.build | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -328,3 +328,3 @@
-if (cc.sizeof('void *') < 8) and (have_system or have_user)
+if (cc.sizeof('void *') < 8) and (have_system or have_user) and host_machine.system() != 'emscripten'
   error('QEMU emulator requires a 64-bit CPU host architecture. Only tools may be built for 32-bit.')
 endif
